Adapted Julia numerical routines
-------------------------------

The ConScape.jl contributors authored the upstream numerical routines used
by _paired_metric_surfaces() and _streamed_default_surfaces() in
inst/extdata/conscape.jl (extdata/conscape.jl in an installed package).
Upstream project: https://github.com/ConScape/ConScape.jl
Upstream license: GNU General Public License version 2.

Source files and routines:
* src/gridrsp.jl: expected_cost(), connected_habitat(), and metric dispatch.
* src/randomizedshortestpath.jl: RSP_expected_cost(),
  RSP_betweenness_kweighted(), and connected_habitat().

Inspected upstream source: ConScape 0.3.0, sensitivity build with git-tree SHA-1
1534b7983fcf3f52d1e84e2d148625342842d614. Numerical equivalence was also tested
against registered ConScape 0.3.0, git-tree SHA-1
b0d387e05e5135e7375e33718cdcb466117c7bee.

ConScapeRtools adaptations, 2026-10-08: share proximity calculations between
metrics; solve target columns in bounded blocks; reuse a sparse factorization
for forward and transposed solves; accumulate per-target contributions; and
retain upstream weighting, diagonal correction, and numerical safeguards.
These are modified implementations, not unmodified upstream source. The
ConScapeRtools authors are responsible for the adaptations.

The adaptations first appeared in version 0.4.31. Version 0.4.32 corrects the
package license declaration and supplies this attribution. The prior MIT-only
declaration did not grant MIT rights to the upstream-derived routines.

